cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived MA2A release."
title: "MA2A: Memoria.ia Agent-to-Agent Protocol"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-rc1"
date-released: 2026-08-21
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22048589"
authors:
  - family-names: "Matos"
    given-names: "Marcelo Roldão"
abstract: >-
  MA2A (Memoria.ia Agent-to-Agent) is an experimental protocol and reference
  implementation for deterministic trajectory and state synchronization among
  autonomous agents, edge devices, robots, IoT systems, and organizational
  Memoria.ia nodes. The architecture separates edge-side cognition from
  synchronization and includes deterministic conflict handling and an Ed25519
  organizational PKI and challenge-response handshake.
repository-code: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/ma2a"
keywords:
  - "agent-to-agent"
  - "resolutive memory"
  - "deterministic synchronization"
  - "edge AI"
  - "PKI"
  - "multi-agent systems"
